Small parity and correctness gaps found across two audits, grouped because each
is a few lines and they all live in `Task.pm`/`Config.pm`.

**Body "0" is swallowed** — `Task.pm:135` and `:126` both test `if $self->body`,
so a body of `0` is falsy and dropped:

    karr create "Zero body" --body 0
    karr show 1        -> no body
    karr show 1 --json -> no "body" key

kanban-md tests `t.Body != ""` (`internal/task/file.go:52`).

**Body loses a trailing newline per ref round trip** — `Git.pm:263` chomps the
blob and `Task.pm:145` additionally strips `s/\n$//`. The `save`/`from_file` path
does not chomp, so the two storage paths are not equivalent.

**`claim_timeout` silently becomes 1h for compound durations** —
`Role/ClaimTimeout.pm:15-21` only understands `^\d+h$` and `^\d+m$`, everything
else falls back to 3600. kanban-md uses `time.ParseDuration`, so an imported
config with `claim_timeout: 1h30m` means 90 minutes there and 60 here.

**Slug truncation differs** — `Task.pm:78` cuts hard at 50 characters; Go trims
to the last word boundary and strips leftover dashes
(`internal/task/slug.go:22-30`):

    karr: 001-implement-the-new-authentication-subsystem-with-to.md
    go:   001-implement-the-new-authentication-subsystem-with.md

In a shared `tasks/` directory that means two files for the same task id.

**No config validation on the import/restore path** — `karr config set` validates
(`Cmd/Config.pm:98-105`), a config arriving through `import` does not:

    # config.yml with  defaults: {status: nonexistent, priority: bogus}
    karr create "X" -> rc=0;  karr show 1 -> Status: nonexistent / Priority: bogus

And `karr config show` dies raw on a broken schema:
`Can't use string ("42") as an ARRAY ref while "strict refs" in use at Cmd/Config.pm line 121`.
Fixed and merged into main (3dac607); full suite green at 93 files / 630 tests.
Reproduced before the fix, regression test verified to fail against the pre-fix
code. Note the #68 trigger change: started is now stamped on the first move out
of the FIRST CONFIGURED status, per kanban-md lifecycle.go, not out of the
literal in-progress.
